+      "2014 spell procedures": "Command, at will. Action, 60 ft., one visible creature. On a failed DC 13 Wisdom save it follows a one-word order on its next turn. It must understand the language. Undead and directly harmful commands are ineligible. The spell ends if the target cannot comply. The DM resolves orders outside the listed examples. Approach ends the turn when it reaches within 5 ft. of the swarm by the shortest route. Drop ends the turn after dropping held items. Flee spends the turn moving away as quickly as it can. Grovel drops it prone and ends the turn. Halt prevents movement and actions, with minimum flight allowed if needed to stay aloft.\nComprehend Languages, at will. Action, self, 1 hour. Understand literal spoken language the swarm hears and writing it sees while touching the written surface. Read one page per minute. It cannot decode ciphers or signs outside a written language.\nDetect Thoughts, at will. Action, self, concentration up to 1 minute. Read the surface thoughts of a visible creature within 30 ft. The creature must have Intelligence 4 or higher and speak a language. On a later action, switch targets or probe deeper. A probe alerts the target, which makes a DC 13 Wisdom save. Success ends the spell. Failure reveals reasoning, emotional state, and a major concern. A probed creature can use an action to end the spell by winning an Intelligence contest against the swarm while it remains the focus. On casting or as an action the swarm can also search for eligible unseen minds within 30 ft., then read them while in range. Two feet of rock, 2 inches of non-lead metal, or a thin sheet of lead blocks that search.\nConfusion, 1/day. Action, 90 ft., concentration up to 1 minute. Each creature in a 10-ft.-radius sphere around a point in range makes a DC 13 Wisdom save. A failure prevents reactions and requires a d10 at the start of each turn. On 1, roll a d8 for direction and spend all movement going that way without acting. On 2–6, the creature stays still and does nothing. On 7–8, it spends its action on one melee attack against a random creature in reach. If there is none, it does nothing. On 9–10, it moves and acts as usual. A DC 13 Wisdom save at the end of its turn ends the effect on that creature.\nDominate Monster, 1/day. Action, 60 ft., a visible creature, concentration up to 1 hour. The target makes a DC 13 Wisdom save, with advantage if the swarm or its allies are fighting it. Failure charms it. While conscious and on the same plane, the swarm can issue simple commands by telepathy without an action. If orders run out it protects itself. The swarm can spend an action for precise control through the end of its next turn and can spend its own reaction to direct the target’s reaction. Each time the target takes damage, another DC 13 Wisdom save can end the spell.",
+      "HP threshold": "With its printed maximum of 36 HP, the swarm can cast at 19 HP or more. At 18 HP or less, use the smaller Bites damage.",
+      "Encounter ecology": "The rats combine their memories and minds when they swarm and communicate as one. A rat separated from the swarm begins with Intelligence 15, loses 1 Intelligence per day to a minimum of 4, and returns to 15 when it rejoins any such swarm. Illithid colonies can receive a swarm’s reports within the elder brain’s telepathic range.",
+      "Source notes": "The swarm’s Telepathic Shroud covers all divination spells. The same block lists Detect Thoughts and Comprehend Languages, both self-range divinations, with no explicit self-cast exception. Both printed rules are retained.\nThe 2014 Command language and harmful-order restrictions still apply. Volo grants component-free casting and separately lists telepathy 30 ft."
